{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02669",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.87,
      "end_seconds": 5.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Doctor? Hello, I hope this is the right time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.5,
      "end_seconds": 11.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.29,
      "end_seconds": 22.43,
      "duration_seconds": 10.14,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come. We came because of breathlessness building over weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.16,
      "end_seconds": 26.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.25,
      "end_seconds": 32.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Let me think, about two weeks, give or take."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 32.93,
      "end_seconds": 37.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Oh, hm, I'd say more like three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.02,
      "end_seconds": 42.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly two to three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.63,
      "end_seconds": 44.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Yeah, roughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.31,
      "end_seconds": 48.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Understood. How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.42,
      "end_seconds": 51.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "I'd call it mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.42,
      "end_seconds": 55.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Have you had weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.51,
      "end_seconds": 76.15,
      "duration_seconds": 19.64,
      "text": "Yes, uh, I have. As for dull ache on one side of the chest, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.85,
      "end_seconds": 79.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "How frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.23,
      "end_seconds": 83.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "It just comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.28,
      "end_seconds": 91.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "Right, right. Have you had breathlessness building over weeks before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.1,
      "end_seconds": 105.64,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last year, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.33,
      "end_seconds": 120.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.26,
      "text": "A few quick ones: night sweats, fever, coughing up blood or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.67,
      "end_seconds": 129.17,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "Well, no night sweats, fever, coughing up blood or leg swelling, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.24,
      "end_seconds": 133.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.35,
      "end_seconds": 139.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Actually, uh, no, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.66,
      "end_seconds": 144.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Alright, what do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.53,
      "end_seconds": 161.91,
      "duration_seconds": 16.38,
      "text": "Losartan. I take it 50 milligrams, once a day for my blood pressure. So, you know, it's something called allo... allopurinol, 100 milligrams, maybe, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.34,
      "end_seconds": 166.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.44,
      "end_seconds": 171.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "No, um, it's at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.67,
      "end_seconds": 176.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.43,
      "end_seconds": 185.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Oh, um, just a meniscus repair on my knee, four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.84,
      "end_seconds": 188.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.62,
      "end_seconds": 193.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.11,
      "end_seconds": 195.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "And your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.63,
      "end_seconds": 204.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.88,
      "end_seconds": 209.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.8,
      "end_seconds": 214.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.06,
      "end_seconds": 234.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "Okay, before we go further, any allergies? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.55,
      "end_seconds": 239.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.82,
      "end_seconds": 243.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.97,
      "end_seconds": 248.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "I, I have high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.47,
      "end_seconds": 252.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.42,
      "end_seconds": 261.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "Yes, gout. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.03,
      "end_seconds": 267.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. Alright, I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.6,
      "end_seconds": 278.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.05,
      "end_seconds": 302.52,
      "duration_seconds": 8.47,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 90 percent, BP is 135 over 72, respiratory rate 24, heart rate 88."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.54,
      "end_seconds": 307.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.47,
      "end_seconds": 311.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Right, I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.5,
      "end_seconds": 333.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "There is dullness to percussion and reduced breath sounds at the right base."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.48,
      "end_seconds": 341.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Right, thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.56,
      "end_seconds": 358.58,
      "duration_seconds": 9.02,
      "text": "Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had breathlessness building over weeks, mild, and no coughing up blood or night sweats."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.13,
      "end_seconds": 360.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Mm, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.03,
      "end_seconds": 373.45,
      "duration_seconds": 10.42,
      "text": "A CT scan of the chest is what I'd like next, for pleural effusion. A pleural fluid sample is what I'd like next, for pleural effusion."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.69,
      "end_seconds": 377.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "How long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.6,
      "end_seconds": 399.65,
      "duration_seconds": 21.05,
      "text": "I am arranging an urgent chest clinic review. I'd like you to see the chest clinic as well, and I'll write the referral. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 400.52,
      "end_seconds": 405.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Okay, you know, I'll look out for that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 409.44,
      "end_seconds": 420.22,
      "duration_seconds": 10.78,
      "text": "Please come and see me after the scan. Can you tell me the plan back in your own words, so I know I've explained it clearly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 422.26,
      "end_seconds": 427.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "So, I come back after the scan. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 428.07,
      "end_seconds": 433.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 435.05,
      "end_seconds": 438.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
}